{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>My mouth, Your righteousness</b> — which You did for others and with me in former days, and the deliverances You wrought." "<b>For I do not know</b> — like (Exodus 34:9): \"for it is a stiff-necked people,\" even though I do not know their number. And חולם [holem] is spelled defectively [ספורות] in place of שורק [male spelling], on the pattern of גבורות."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 71, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra discusses the spelling of מספר (number): the expected plene form would have a vav (שורק = ו as mater lectionis), but the text spells it defectively with only a holem. The reference to גבורות as an analogous defective spelling is obscure and possibly textually corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:55.575206160Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}